Euphoria@junkpile.demon.co.uk (Ian Crowther) writes:

>Why is is it assumed that a multihack MUST preserve the move for move
>timing of original nethack, this is the first thing that must be removed
>before the game can be made multi user..
>Consider that a normal speed player/monster might get to execute a command
>every second (I'm dreaming the numbers here so don't hassle me on them)
>a fast player/monster every 2/3 second or similar, then you are perfectly
>able to play at a speed similar to the original nethack.  

Think again.  At even 1 move ever 1/4 second, it would take 20 seconds
to move from one side of the maze to the other, and you'd have no chance of
using a wand or anything other than a bash & slash weapon at that rate.


I have done work on a multi-player hack-style game of my own, and
it really is a difficult proposition.

Making NetHack a real-time game would spoil it for most of us.  If we
want an arcade hack&slash, there are dozens existing already.  They all
suck, IMO... because they are realtime.

